WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:07.010
<v ->Regulating our emotions isn't always easy.</v>

2
00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:09.780
It's hard not to be overwhelmed when we're stressed,

3
00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:11.480
lash out when we're angry,

4
00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:13.770
or feel defeated when we fail.

5
00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:16.060
But by boosting your self-regulation,

6
00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:18.060
you can control your emotions,

7
00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.470
rather than letting them control you.

8
00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:23.820
It's a useful skill, so let's take a look

9
00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:26.030
at the elements of self-regulation

10
00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:28.933
and how you can improve your self-regulation skills.

11
00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:34.110
First, self-regulation is made up of five elements.

12
00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:36.550
To start, there's self-control,

13
00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:39.410
which is your ability to control your feelings.

14
00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:40.810
With high self-control,

15
00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:43.090
you can remain rational and levelheaded,

16
00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:45.140
even when your emotions are running high.

17
00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:49.400
Second, there's trustworthiness.

18
00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.200
When you regulate your emotions,

19
00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:53.810
you're less likely to act impulsively.

20
00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:57.240
You act consistently and according to your values,

21
00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:00.220
and that helps others trust your behavior.

22
00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:03.040
Third, there's conscientiousness,

23
00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:06.310
which is about being disciplined and responsible.

24
00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:09.280
Rather than blaming external factors for your actions,

25
00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:12.113
you take responsibility for your performance.

26
00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:15.990
Fourth, there's a adaptability,

27
00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:17.750
which refers to how well you handle

28
00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:20.530
change and unexpected stress.

29
00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:23.230
Without this quality, you may crack under pressure

30
00:01:23.230 --> 00:01:27.030
or express high anxiety, stress, and worry.

31
00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:29.520
And finally, there's innovation.

32
00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:31.170
With strong self-regulation,

33
00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:34.050
you're more likely to see challenges as opportunities,

34
00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:37.690
and be open to new, innovative ideas.

35
00:01:37.690 --> 00:01:41.700
So, how can you improve your self-regulation?

36
00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:43.650
Rather than avoiding your feelings,

37
00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:45.910
you'll need to confront them head-on.

38
00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:47.633
Here are five tips.

39
00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:50.870
The first tip for improving your self-regulation

40
00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:52.860
is to prepare for the emotion.

41
00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:55.070
If you need to walk into a tough conversation,

42
00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:57.390
or you know you have a challenging day ahead,

43
00:01:57.390 --> 00:01:59.390
think about how you can calm yourself down

44
00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:00.543
before that event.

45
00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:03.690
Prepare for your emotional reactions,

46
00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:06.353
and you'll be less likely to get caught off-guard.

47
00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:11.600
Second, practice mindful observation.

48
00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:13.450
Rather than burying your feelings,

49
00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:15.090
mindfully accept them.

50
00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:16.990
Recognize why you're feeling the way you are,

51
00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:18.503
and don't judge that emotion.

52
00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:23.242
Third, take time to STOPP,

53
00:02:23.242 --> 00:02:28.140
which is an acronym that stands for stop, take a breath,

54
00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:31.303
observe, pull back, and proceed.

55
00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:35.120
When your emotions are spinning,

56
00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:38.690
pause, breathe in, observe how you're feeling,

57
00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:41.310
and take a step back before responding.

58
00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:44.400
Then, once you've evaluated that bigger picture,

59
00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:47.440
proceed with the most appropriate action.

60
00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:50.220
Fourth, practice letting go.

61
00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:52.080
When we hold onto negative emotions,

62
00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:54.800
we often escalate our sensitivity to them.

63
00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:57.470
So, instead, try to recognize

64
00:02:57.470 --> 00:02:58.770
that something happened,

65
00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:00.580
feel grateful for what you've learned,

66
00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:03.790
and then think toward the future.

67
00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:06.130
Finally, reframe your thoughts

68
00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:08.140
through cognitive reappraisal,

69
00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:10.550
which involves readjusting your mindset.

70
00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:12.350
Whether you're stuck in traffic,

71
00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:14.100
dealing with an unfocused employee,

72
00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:16.850
or feeling disrespected, there are a lot of ways

73
00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:18.890
to interpret the same situation.

74
00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:21.390
And with cognitive reappraisal,

75
00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:24.030
you can choose the healthiest interpretation

76
00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:26.083
by changing your thought patterns.

77
00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:31.130
So, the next time your emotions are running high,

78
00:03:31.130 --> 00:03:33.710
remind yourself that you're in control.

79
00:03:33.710 --> 00:03:36.240
Remember these tips, and you can improve

80
00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:37.830
your self-regulation skills

81
00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:40.083
and stay in the emotional driver's seat.

